...and 0 pieces of gold, after 14303 moves.


Very good time, I think, when one considers that I had no wishes before the 
castle.  Even so there were many areas were I wasted turns with stupidity or 
inefficiency -- without those I'd have cut the time to under 13k moves, and 
then maybe different strategic choices could have improved it further.  But 
the easiest way to beat my time is to find a wand of wishing on level two.  


I didn't find many exceptional items in the early game:

- two large potion shops that made good polyfodder and holy water
- wand of polymorph with 6 charges (but read on)
- amulet of reflection in Sokoban and bag of holding soon after
---> SPEED BOOTS <--- fairly early.  Turn 4000, or maybe turn 2000.  Yes, 
Tommi, they are very good.


Minetown temple was cross-aligned.  There wasn't much in the shops.  Minesend 
was only the second-best version.  I returned to Minetown and stood outside 
the temple and zapped the polymorph wand at the priest.  He resisted the 
first charge and then turned into an easily-killed jellyfish.  (In fact I 
avoided murder entirely this game; there was no easy way to kill the 
shopkeepers early, and no reason to since the priest was dead.)  I converted 
the altar, prayed for holy water, and then left Minetown for good.

I polypiled in Sokoban, and very luckily produced a scroll of charging on 
what would otherwise have been my last zap.  I was only able to recharge the 
wand once, because no magic marker.  Afterwards I did some alchemy and 
boosted HP past 100.

Dug downwards using wand and pickaxe until I saw some chickatrices.  I got a 
corpse and continued straight down.  Later there was a cockatrice nest, so I 
took a corpse from there also since it would be fresher.  On the Medusa level 
I dug down without removing my blindfold and got wet once.

The most dangerous monsters at the castle were the Xorns (used a wand of 
lightning and darts on them) and an air elemental (wand of teleport).  The 
rubber chicken ran out after I had killed all but about 15 soldiers and a few 
random monsters.  Yes, there was a soldier with a wand of death.

The castle throne gave my first wish: the Eye.  I retreated to Sokoban with 
the 0:1 wand, and wished for:
- holy magic marker
- unholy magic marker
- book of polymorph
- +3 helm of brilliance
- magic marker

I did not need to wish for scrolls of genocide since the polypile had 
produced one.  I wasted many turns trying to cast polymorph at 84% fail, then 
realized I should train Matter skill up with wizard lock first.

I explored the levels between Sokoban and the Castle, and found a bones file 
with two magic lamps, water walking boots, dex gloves, more...

<rast> found your bones file where you died in a shop on like lvl 15
<rast> thx for the magic lamps, sucka!
<greycat> dead barbarian, Dlvl:19, general store, two magic lamps (one lit), 
etc.?  Grrr.
<greycat> A fucking ettin showed up in the shop door, and killed me.

I spent both lamps on magic markers.  

There was a co-aligned temple, so I donated 4 times for 7 points of 
protection, and also sacrificed to max Luck.

Kaen died to a wand of death before he could pick up the Eyes.

I cleared the Valley and teleported to the bottom, then realized I couldn't 
do much without spell of magic mapping, so returned to Sokoban and polypiled 
madly for it.  Then I realized I'd had the spell all along.  That is what I 
mean about wasted turns through stupidity.

Other mistakes:

Didn't curse any of my !oGL for the Sanctum and Valley.
Polypiled the random HoOA instead of saving it for Astral.
Didn't summoned cockatrices on Astral until an Archon showed up and things 
got crowded.  Next time it will be my first action upon arriving.

The correct altar was the second one I tried.  My only conduct was 
polyselfless.  I wasn't trying for weaponless but I had it except for pickaxe 
incidents.

